msgid "narration/narrationText/ls_narration_1"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $highlightText}}TOP SECRET{{/}}{{titleParagraph}}{{@ class "
"$highlightText}}SECTOR: N-07 (\"Aurora\" Perimeter){{/}}{{pargraphStart}}Our"
" prediction was correct. Station observers recorded the anomaly's approach "
"11 days prior to the event. For the first time, we saw it "
"coming.{{pargraphStart}}During the calm before the storm, production of "
"ATLAS complexes was standardized. New modules are assembled faster and "
"calibrated more precisely. We carried out training, ran through formations, "
"and prepared back-up squads. Full alert.{{pargraphStart}}But the anomaly had"
" its own plans.{{pargraphStart}}The Funnel didn't open in the predicted "
"sector. It appeared here, in a remote northern region, far from the deployed"
" infrastructure. It's not clear why this location was chosen. Nothing in the"
" models had indicated this area. Emergency redeployment was initiated "
"immediately, but the terrain and distance aren't in our favor. Some vehicles"
" and squads will arrive late.{{pargraphStart}}Every ATLAS complex we managed"
" to deliver is now indispensable.{{pargraphStart}}This time, we were ready "
"for combat. But for combat in a different "
"location.{{pargraphStart}}SIGNATURE: CURATOR (PROJECT M)"

msgid "narration/narrationText/ls_narration_2"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $highlightText}}Analytical Memo 27/C \"INVASION LOCATION "
"SELECTION\"{{/}}{{titleParagraph}}For internal use. \"Restricted Access\" "
"stamp.{{pargraphStart}}I ask a question I'm obliged to answer, but can't: "
"Why here?{{pargraphStart}}This region has no strategic value for the Funnel."
" There's nothing here. No infrastructure, no settlements. Only a non-"
"operational military base on the island. Echo tanks can't cross the sea. So "
"why capture a location they can't attack from? {{pargraphStart}}I requested "
"the region's full operational history. The reply was heavily redacted. Whole"
" sections had been blanked out. A second request was sent back with the note"
" \"access restricted by the authority of {{@ class "
"$highlightSecondaryText}}[DATA REMOVED]{{/}}.\" I, the head of the research "
"department, whose recommendations determine this sector's defense strategy, "
"am being denied information about this territory!{{pargraphStart}}Here's "
"what I can deduce from field data: the Funnel's behavior doesn't correspond "
"to what we observed in sector R-22. New types of echo tanks that we haven't "
"encountered before have appeared. They correspond in function to our long-"
"range tank destroyers and are extremely effective on this kind of terrain. "
"The opponent has learned from our tactics and taken countermeasures. Now "
"it's our turn to adapt.{{pargraphStart}}It might be that it needs this "
"place. Or maybe what's underneath it.{{pargraphStart}}I don't know. And it "
"worries me that somebody knows, but won't say.{{pargraphStart}}SIGNATURE: "
"CURATOR (PROJECT M)"

msgid "narration/narrationText/ls_narration_3"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $highlightText}}CURATOR'S PERSONAL "
"RECORD{{/}}{{pargraphStart}}I've reviewed my own hypotheses. All "
"three.{{pargraphStart}}  1. The anomaly seeks to destroy us. "
"{{pargraphStart}}  2. The anomaly is experimenting. It researches our "
"tactics, studies our response, adjusts, and learns.{{pargraphStart}}  3. The"
" anomaly is training. Each wave is a drill of its new tactics; each battle "
"is training in field conditions.{{pargraphStart}}All three hypotheses share "
"the assumption that we are the target of this invasion.{{pargraphStart}}But "
"what if we aren't?{{pargraphStart}}What if the anomaly is doing something "
"else, and we're simply standing in its way? Like an ant nest flooded while a"
" road's being built. The builder doesn't wage war with the ants. It simply "
"doesn't notice them.{{pargraphStart}}You can stop an enemy who wants to "
"destroy you. You can negotiate with them. But you can't scare something that"
" doesn't acknowledge your existence; you can't outsmart it. It can't be "
"stopped. Because you were never part of its calculations.{{pargraphStart}}I "
"think we've been asking the wrong question. We shouldn't be asking why it's "
"attacking us, but whether it notices us at all.{{pargraphStart}}SIGNATURE: "
"CURATOR (PROJECT M)"

msgid "narration/narrationText/ls_narration_4"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $highlightText}}FINAL REPORT{{/}}{{titleParagraph}}{{@ class "
"$highlightText}}STATUS: DECLASSIFIED (PARTLY){{/}}{{pargraphStart}}At 03:47,"
" the Funnel collapsed. The anomaly's activity stopped. The sector is "
"clear.{{pargraphStart}}In the final seconds before the collapse, ATLAS "
"meters registered an energy surge that exceeded all previously recorded "
"values. The crews observed a short-lived physical manifestation in the "
"center of the anomaly, which lasted no longer than 12 seconds. After that, "
"the Funnel closed. {{pargraphStart}}Official statement: The incident is "
"over. The territory has been successfully defended. The quarantine has been "
"lifted from the sector.{{pargraphStart}}{{@ class $highlightText}}CURATOR'S "
"PERSONAL NOTE (Only for special reserves){{/}}{{pargraphStart}}We didn't "
"win. It finished.{{pargraphStart}}This wasn't an invasion. It was a cover. A"
" protective perimeter around what manifested in the Funnel's center seconds "
"before its collapse.{{pargraphStart}}Dozens of Obelisks appeared "
"simultaneously. We still don't know what they were doing. ATLAS recorded all"
" the parameters, but it will take time to interpret them. We know one thing "
"with near certainty: the anomaly completed some kind of "
"process.{{pargraphStart}}Whatever it was doing, we need to prepare for the "
"next attack. We have enough data now. Our engineers are already going "
"through the recordings, and, to be honest, I've never seen them so excited. "
"They think we can seriously strengthen our vehicles. We need to do so before"
" the Funnel returns. {{pargraphStart}}I can't stop thinking about one thing:"
" if this happened here and lasted such a short time, how many times has it "
"happened before? In places where there was no ATLAS, no one to see it "
"happening...{{pargraphStart}}SIGNATURE: CURATOR (PROJECT M)"

